\f2\b0 : Jones shows more emotional vulnerability (weeping at the jukebox) than Smith, who primarily displays anger and disgust.\

\f3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	1	
\f1\b 	2	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Self-Awareness
\f2\b0 : Smith eventually gains awareness of his prison and seeks freedom; Jones shows no signs of recognizing the restrictive nature of his role.\

\f3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	1	
\f1\b 	3	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Evolution
\f2\b0 : Smith evolves dramatically throughout the Matrix trilogy; Jones is currently more static.\

\f3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	1	
\f1\b 	4	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Independence
\f2\b0 : Smith ultimately breaks from his programming; Jones remains loyal to authority.\

\f3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	1	
\f1\b 	5	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Internal Conflict
\f2\b0 : Jones struggles with the gospel music "infection," showing internal conflict absent in early Smith.\

\f3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	1	
\f1\b 	6	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
