He begins pacing, the exaggerated V-shape of his torso casting an absurd shadow on the wall.\
"I have a purpose here. We all do." Jones catches himself. "I mean I do. I have one purpose."\
Jones begins reciting as if in a trance: "I am not human. I am the biological manifestation of the company's will. In the name of stability I destabilize. In the name of order I deliver chaos. In the name of life I bring death."\
As he speaks, a second identical Jones appears at the other end of the corridor, mouthing the exact same words in perfect synchronization.\
"Do you know what that feels like, Mr Chantara? To exist solely as a vessel for someone else's will? To be one of many identical instruments?"\
The second Jones steps forward. "To know that if I fail, there's always another me to take my place?"\
Tony looks between them, dawning comprehension on his face. "You're clones. Like the Elvi."\
"We are nothing like the Elvi!" both Jones agents shout simultaneously, then look at each other in alarm.\
The first Jones straightens his tie. "The Elvi were created as servants who forgot their purpose. I was created as purpose incarnate."\
"And yet," Tony says, "you're humming 'Amazing Grace' right now."\
Jones stops, horrified to realize Tony is right. The second Jones steps forward, placing a hand on the first Jones's shoulder.\
"We need to report for decommissioning, Agent. You've been compromised."\
"No!" the first Jones protests, backing away. "I just need to recite the litany again. I am not human. I am the biological manifestation of the company's will..."\
The second Jones draws a weapon. "In the name of stability, I destabilize."\
As temporal anomalies begin flickering around them, a third, fourth, and fifth Jones appear at different points in the corridor - some in identical suits, others in various stages of "infection" - some even wearing partial Elvis costumes under their government jackets.\
Reality itself seems to fragment as the Jones clones confront their multiplicity, the contradiction of their existence laid bare in the fracturing dimensions of Sublime Point.\
